    "card5_title": "How to Verify and Inspect JWT Signatures in Browser Memory (Zero Server Uploads)",
    "card5_excerpt": "Pasting production JSON Web Tokens and secrets into online debuggers leaks credentials to CDN logs and analytics. Learn how to verify HS256 and RS256 signatures 100% locally in browser RAM using the native Web Crypto API.",
    "card5_author": "By Mohamed Hajjami",
    "card5_date": "Oct 2026",
    "card5_cta": "Read Guide",
    "a5_nav_launch": "Launch JWT Decoder",
    "a5_breadcrumb_blog": "Blog",
    "a5_breadcrumb_cat": "Security & Cryptography",
    "a5_badge_cat": "Security & Cryptography",
    "a5_badge_verified": "100% In-Browser Execution â€¢ 0 Bytes Uploaded",
    "a5_h1": "How to Verify and Inspect JWT Signatures in Browser Memory (Zero Server Uploads)",
    "a5_lead": "Pasting production JSON Web Tokens (RFC 7519) and HMAC secrets into conventional online debuggers exposes bearer credentials to edge CDN logs, third-party analytics, and session interception. Discover how native Web Crypto API cryptographic primitives (SubtleCrypto) decode, validate claims, and verify signatures entirely within local browser RAM with zero network requests.",
    "a5_meta_author_label": "Author: ",
    "a5_meta_author_val": "Mohamed Hajjami",
    "a5_meta_pub_label": "Published: ",
    "a5_meta_pub_val": "October 14, 2026",
    "a5_meta_time_label": "Read Time: ",
    "a5_meta_time_val": "5 min read",
